# MCSP Kbuild Module Integration 0.54

Status: Constructive Linux module-build experiment
Qualification: Under Conditional Experiment
Parent:
- LINUX-KERNEL-OBJECT-PROJECTION-0.53.mcsp

## Objective

Demonstrate that a qualified MCSP kernel-object projection can participate in the
Linux Kbuild module pipeline and be packaged into a loadable-module artifact (.ko)
without loading or executing that module.

Linux module machinery is a realization boundary. It is not MCSP semantic authority.

## Composition

    MCSP semantic obligation
      -> MCSP Assembler
      -> mcsp_kernel_object.o
      -> minimal Linux module adapter
      -> Kbuild / modpost
      -> mcsp_probe.ko
      -> static qualification

The adapter exists only to satisfy the Linux module interface. It must not redefine
the MCSP semantic obligation.

## Bounded MCSP symbol

    mcsp_exclusive_u64

The adapter may call this symbol to establish link integration.

## 0.54 requirements

The resulting .ko SHALL:
- be ELF64 x86-64 relocatable/module artifact;
- contain the MCSP symbol;
- contain Linux module init/exit metadata required by Kbuild;
- pass modpost/build for the running kernel headers;
- preserve the MCSP object as an assembly-owned component;
- contain no userspace _start entry;
- not be loaded during qualification.

## Boundary

0.54 qualifies build/link integration only.

It does not qualify:
- insmod/modprobe;
- module initialization inside the running kernel;
- kernel-space execution of MCSP;
- driver registration;
- hardware access;
- production safety;
- kernel-version portability;
- module signing/enforcement compatibility.

Loading is a separate privileged authorization boundary.
